  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the propagation chain found in the source:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 `PostStartHook()` registers `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"`. It starts both the ClusterIP repair loop (`p.startServiceClusterIPRepair`, which for the `MultiCIDRServiceAllocator` path is `serviceipallocatorcontroller.NewRepairIPAddress(...).RunUntil`) and the NodePort repair loop concurrently via `async.Runner`, waits on a `sync.WaitGroup` for both `onFirstSuccess` callbacks, and if neither fires within **1 minute**, returns `goerrors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` \u2014 this is the exact string in the ticket.\n\n2. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go`** \u2014 `runPostStartHook` calls `klog.Fatalf(\"PostStartHook %q failed: %v\", name, err)` when the hook returns an error, which **crashes the process** (matches the log line format exactly). The `done` channel backing that hook is wired into `postStartHookHealthz`, registered as a readyz/healthz/livez check named `poststarthook/<name>`.\n\n3. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 `RunUntil`'s `runOnce()`/`doRunOnce()` calls `syncService`, which on a missing IPAddress does `r.client.NetworkingV1beta1().IPAddresses().Create(...)`. If that Create errors, `doRunOnce` returns the error unwrapped (not just a conflict, so `retry.RetryOnConflict` doesn't retry it), `runOnce()` fails, `RunUntil` logs it and returns **without calling `onFirstSuccess`** \u2014 so the WaitGroup is never satisfied.\n\n4. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/policy/generic/plugin.go`** \u2014 the ValidatingAdmissionPolicy/MutatingAdmissionPolicy admission plugin's `Dispatch()` gates on `c.WaitForReady()` (namespace informer + policy source synced) and returns `admission.NewForbidden(a, fmt.Errorf(\"not yet ready to handle request\"))` if not \u2014 this matches the `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"10.211.95.185\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request` error. Unlike `NamespaceLifecycle` (`admission.go`, which short-circuits non-namespaced resources like IPAddress before its own `WaitForReady` check), this generic policy plugin applies to cluster-scoped resources too, so it's the plausible source of the forbidden error hitting IPAddress creates.\n\n**The race**: during the mixed-version rolling-upgrade window, a freshly-started v1.33 apiserver's admission-plugin informers (namespace/policy-source sync) haven't caught up yet when the repair controller's first reconciliation pass tries to `Create` an `IPAddress`. That create is rejected as \"not yet ready,\" `doRunOnce` fails, `onFirstSuccess` is never signaled, the 1-minute timeout in `storage_core.go` fires, the PostStartHook error triggers `klog.Fatalf` and a crash/restart, and until that hook completes the `informer-sync` and `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` readyz checks (`healthz.go`) keep failing \u2014 making the node unready for the whole mixed-version window, resolving once all nodes (and their admission caches) are fully v1.33 and stay synced long enough for a repair pass to succeed within 60s.",
